# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the checkout platform.
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# LF to CRLF on checkout. A CRLF shebang line fails inside a Linux
# container with "no such file or directory", pointing at the interpreter
# rather than at the line ending, which is a genuinely confusing way to
# discover the problem. scripts/start.sh is the container entrypoint, so
# that failure would be a total outage on a fresh Windows clone.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: the Dockerfile is read by a Linux builder.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
